title: "statement-store: drop a peer's affinity filter when its substream closes"

doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    On the v2 DHT statement path, a peer's affinity filter is dropped when its statement substream
    closes instead of when block sync reports the peer gone. Filters of peers dialed outside the
    sync set no longer accumulate, and a peer that block sync drops while its substream stays open
    keeps receiving statements on its advertised topics.

crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
